@model Edulytics.Web.ViewModels.LessonContent.Grade2Lesson31Page
@using Edulytics.Core.Mathematics.Practice
@{Layout="_StudentLayout";ViewData["Title"]="Grade 2 — Story Problems and Equations";}
<style>
.g2l31{max-width:960px;margin:auto;padding:20px;color:#224052}.g2l31 .panel{background:#fff;border:1px solid #cbdce6;border-radius:12px;padding:20px;margin:16px 0}.g2l31 .grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(180px,1fr));gap:12px}.g2l31 label{display:block;margin:12px 0 5px;font-weight:700}.g2l31 input,.g2l31 textarea{font:inherit;width:100%;max-width:550px;border:1px solid #8096a3;border-radius:8px;padding:10px}.g2l31 .action{background:#0b8096;color:white;border:0;border-radius:8px;padding:12px 20px;font-weight:bold}.g2l31 .ok{border-left:4px solid #2b855c;padding-left:12px}.g2l31 .bad{border-left:4px solid #ba4a59;padding-left:12px}.g2l31 .review{border-left:4px solid #b08833;padding-left:12px}
</style>
<main class="g2l31">
<a asp-controller="StudentPortal" asp-action="Lesson" asp-route-id="@Model.LessonId">← Back to lesson</a>
<h1>Story Problems and Equations</h1>
<p>A story can describe ADDITION even if SUBTRACTION helps calculate its missing number. Label the unknown and compare equations that genuinely match the action and quantities.</p>
<form asp-controller="Grade2Lesson31Activities" asp-action="Submit" method="post">
@Html.AntiForgeryToken()
<input type="hidden" name="curriculumAdoptionId" value="@Model.AdoptionId"/>
<input type="hidden" name="lessonId" value="@Model.LessonId"/>
<section class="panel"><h2>1. Which One Doesn't Belong? — authentic tape diagrams</h2>
<p>Use teacher-presented original A–D diagrams and discuss which represents <strong>27 + ? = 40</strong>.</p>
<label asp-for="Answers.WarmupMissing">Missing addend in27+?=40</label>
<input asp-for="Answers.WarmupMissing" type="number" min="0" max="100" required/>
<label asp-for="Answers.WarmupDiagramReason">What does the ? label mean on the diagram?</label>
<textarea asp-for="Answers.WarmupDiagramReason" rows="2" maxlength="2000"></textarea>
</section>
<section class="panel"><h2>2. Original card sort — story problems and equations</h2>
<p>In a REAL group of2–4 use the authentic story cards A–I from the previous lesson and the printed equation cards. A single story may match multiple true equations; explain why. Card-specific publisher numbers not present in the public source are not invented here.</p>
<label asp-for="Answers.ActualCardMatches">Which genuine printed card matches did you make?</label>
<textarea asp-for="Answers.ActualCardMatches" rows="2" maxlength="2000"></textarea>
<label asp-for="Answers.ActualCardMultipleEquations">Can two printed equation cards match a story? Explain the role of the unknown</label>
<textarea asp-for="Answers.ActualCardMultipleEquations" rows="2" maxlength="2000"></textarea>
</section>
<section class="panel"><h2>3. Four original source story problems</h2>
<div class="grid">
<div><p>Lin STARTED with some seeds, then won36; now64. What did she start with?</p>
<label asp-for="Answers.LinStart">?+36=64</label><input asp-for="Answers.LinStart" type="number" min="0" max="100" required/></div>
<div><p>Andre started32 seeds, won MORE, then had57. How many did he win?</p>
<label asp-for="Answers.AndreWon">32+?=57</label><input asp-for="Answers.AndreWon" type="number" min="0" max="100" required/></div>
<div><p>Diego gathered22 yellow and48 blue seeds. How many altogether?</p>
<label asp-for="Answers.DiegoTotal">22+48=?</label><input asp-for="Answers.DiegoTotal" type="number" min="0" max="100" required/></div>
<div><p>Noah and Kiran gathered92; Noah53. How many did Kiran gather?</p>
<label asp-for="Answers.KiranPart">53+?=92</label><input asp-for="Answers.KiranPart" type="number" min="0" max="100" required/></div>
</div>
<label asp-for="Answers.StoryEquationsAndTapeDiagrams">Describe original tape diagrams and equations, including an addition and subtraction equation that BOTH fit Noah and Kiran</label>
<textarea asp-for="Answers.StoryEquationsAndTapeDiagrams" rows="3" maxlength="2000"></textarea>
</section>
<section class="panel"><h2>4. Original Edulytics independent exit</h2>
<p>These are FIRST-PARTY checks, not the publisher's restricted Match the Equation Cool-down.</p>
<div class="grid">
<div><label asp-for="Answers.FirstPartyStart">?+27=63</label><input asp-for="Answers.FirstPartyStart" type="number" min="0" max="100" required/></div>
<div><label asp-for="Answers.FirstPartyChange">41+?=75</label><input asp-for="Answers.FirstPartyChange" type="number" min="0" max="100" required/></div>
<div><label asp-for="Answers.FirstPartyTotal">18+47=?</label><input asp-for="Answers.FirstPartyTotal" type="number" min="0" max="100" required/></div>
<div><label asp-for="Answers.FirstPartyPart">56+?=91</label><input asp-for="Answers.FirstPartyPart" type="number" min="0" max="100" required/></div>
</div>
<label asp-for="Answers.PartnerSummary">What did your real partner teach you about an equation matching a story?</label>
<textarea asp-for="Answers.PartnerSummary" rows="2" maxlength="2000"></textarea>
<button type="submit" class="action">Check numeric unknowns and show teacher review</button></section>
</form>
@if(Model.Submitted){<section class="panel" aria-live="polite"><h2>Feedback</h2>
@foreach(var r in Model.Feedback){<div class="@(r.Correct==true?"ok":r.Correct==false?"bad":"review")">
<h3>@r.Section</h3><p>@(r.Correct==true?"Math correct":r.Correct==false?"Revisit the unknown":"Teacher observation required"). @r.Feedback</p></div>}
</section>}
<section class="panel"><h2>Teacher rubric</h2><ul>@foreach(var item in UsCcssG2Unit2ThirteenthLessonStoryEquations.TeacherRubric){<li>@item</li>}</ul>
<p>Source IM K–5 2021 G2 U02 L13; CCSS 2.NBT.B.5 and 2.OA.A.1. Real card sort and protected Cool-down not replicated, no official grade.</p>
</section></main>
